@startuml HermesPersistence
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: where hermes keeps its home (sessions, memories, skills, vault) so it survives the sandbox
' covers: defs/hermes/entrypoint.sh (HERMES_HOME block)
' covers: internal/imagetest/hermes_test.go (hmPersistence)
' covers: defs/hermes/harness.manifest (home.mounts)
' covers: internal/manifest/manifest.go (home.mounts validation)
' covers: internal/contract/config_set_test.go (TestHermesDataIsBoundNotCopiedIntoTheAgentHome)
'   the sandbox lifecycle that removes volumes ... _spec/internal/sbx/kit-lifecycle.puml
'
' ── F19 (DONE (wt) 2026-10-17): THE DURABLE HOME IS A DIRECT HOST BIND ─────
' The user asked to "research how to properly mount home data in hermes + sbx
' for F19" (repo-simplification.puml F19). Findings (reported by the
' coordinator): sbx mounts workspaces path-preserving; an image VOLUME is
' per-sandbox and dies at `sbx rm` (as MEASURED below, 2026-09-27); and
' [Unverified] sbx's -v/--volume is experimental and cloud-only. So the durable
' home is the host bind itself, with HERMES_HOME pointed at it — what the
' entrypoint already does (defs/hermes/entrypoint.sh:45).
' MEASURED fix: defs/hermes/harness.manifest's home mount is `host: hermes/data,
' mode: rw` with NO `container:` — the docker-era `container: /proveo-home/data`
' is gone, so config-sync no longer COPIES hermes data into ~/data on every
' launch (the copy was dead weight: HERMES_HOME already points at the bound
' host path). manifest validation accepts an empty container — a direct bind —
' and checks container duplicates only when one is set (manifest.go:273-288).
' Tests: TestHermesDataIsBoundNotCopiedIntoTheAgentHome (config_set_test.go:84,
' reported red before the fix), TestAHomeMountMayOmitItsContainerPath
' (manifest_test.go:366), and TestEveryHarnessHomeMountReachesTheConfigSet
' (config_set_test.go:15), which now counts only mounts that name a container.
'
' ── MEASURED 2026-09-27 (sbx v0.42.1, proveo/hermes:local, v0.21.5) ─────────
' The image sets HERMES_HOME=/opt/data and declares VOLUME /opt/data. sbx backs
' that with a PER-SANDBOX volume on the host:
'   ~/Library/Application Support/com.docker.sandboxes/sandboxes/sandboxd/
'     containerd/root/com.docker.volume.driver.v1.local/volumes/<id>/
' Probe: a fresh sandbox got a new volume id; `sbx rm` deleted it. So every
' successful proveo run (teardown removes the sandbox) and every stale-sandbox
' re-create erased state.db, memories/, skills/, vault/, .env and config.yaml.
'
' The manifest's durable mount (host ~/.proveo/hermes/data) DID reach the
' sandbox — at its HOST path, because sbx mounts workspaces where they live.
' The entrypoint only tested /proveo-home/data (the docker rendering), which
' sbx never creates, so hermes kept writing to the volume and the durable
' folder stayed empty.
'
' ── RULE (updated 2026-10-16) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
' HERMES_HOME is $PROVEO_STATE_HOME/hermes/data — the sbx rendering of the
' manifest's durable mount, at its host path — when it is writable; else the
' image's /opt/data (non-durable), or ~/.hermes for a non-root uid that cannot
' write /opt/data. MEASURED: defs/hermes/entrypoint.sh probes only the
' PROVEO_STATE_HOME path now. The /proveo-home/data candidate (the docker+egress
' rendering) is gone with that backend, and the hermes image test asserts only
' AGENT_BROWSER_EXECUTABLE_PATH there, no /proveo-home/data probe. The manifest
' no longer names a `container:` path at all (F19 above; it named
' /proveo-home/data until 2026-10-17, which sbx ignored). upstream stage2-hook.sh
' reads HERMES_HOME and bootstraps/chowns whatever path it is given.
' One-time move: durable home EMPTY and /opt/data/state.db present ⇒ tar-copy
' /opt/data into it (tar, not cp -a: the home holds live .sock files).
'
' Rescue on 2026-09-27: volume a7796143… copied to ~/.proveo/hermes/data by
' hand (15,828 files, 2 sockets skipped, state.db integrity_check ok), since a
' non-empty durable home disables the automatic move.

node "sbx microVM" as VM {
  component "hermes\nHERMES_HOME" as H
  component "/opt/data\nimage VOLUME" as V
}
folder "host ~/.proveo/hermes/data\n(= $PROVEO_STATE_HOME/hermes/data)" as D
folder "sbx volume <id>\ndeleted by sbx rm" as SV

H --> D : durable (after this fix)
V --> SV
H ..> V : before: every run started over

note right of D
  **Durable means outside the sandbox.**
  The folder survives sbx rm, so
  sessions, skills and the vault
  outlive every run.
end note
' ── WRITE SAFE ROOT (2026-09-28) ───────────────────────────────────────────
' The upstream image sets ENV HERMES_WRITE_SAFE_ROOT=/opt/data, and
' agent/file_safety.py denies write_file/patch outside it (os.pathsep list).
' Under sbx /opt/data is the VM's own volume: the first scheduled rehearsal
' could not write <workspace>/report.md ("Write denied … outside
' HERMES_WRITE_SAFE_ROOT"), wrote /opt/data/muse-lineup/report.md instead,
' and that copy dies with the sandbox. The entrypoint now appends the
' workspace ($(pwd) after set_working_directory) and HERMES_HOME (the durable
' home) to the list. The terminal tool was never restricted by it.
@enduml
